#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Graphene: one sheet of graphite, written by hand for Crystal Builder.
#
# Not a deposition -- a monolayer has none.  The in-plane cell is
# graphite's (a = 2.46 A, C-C 1.42 A); c = 20 A is vacuum, so the
# sheet's images along c are 20 A apart and nothing bonds across them.
# Both carbons are one site, 2c of P6/mmm.  Public domain, like the
# COD files beside it.
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
data_graphene
_chemical_name_common            graphene
_chemical_formula_sum            'C'
_space_group_IT_number           191
_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M   'P 6/m m m'
_symmetry_space_group_name_Hall  '-P 6 2'
_cell_length_a                   2.46
_cell_length_b                   2.46
_cell_length_c                   20.0
_cell_angle_alpha                90
_cell_angle_beta                 90
_cell_angle_gamma                120
_cell_formula_units_Z            2
loop_
_atom_site_label
_atom_site_type_symbol
_atom_site_fract_x
_atom_site_fract_y
_atom_site_fract_z
_atom_site_occupancy
C1 C 0.33333 0.66667 0.00000 1.0
